      "side": 1,
      "message": "Per [TCPCI R2.0 v1.2] spec, COMMAND.I2CIDLE (the spec superset for \u0027sleep\u0027) has no allowances for abnormal delays waking from sleep.\n\n\u003e COMMAND.I2Cidle is decoupled from other Alert status detection mechanisms (such as CC_STATUS, POWER_STATUS, RECEIVE_DETECT, etc). For example, writing COMMAND.\nI2Cidle has no effect on ALERT.CcStatus, or the CC_STATUS register behavior. CC_STATUS detection may be disabled by writing to the ROLE_CONTROL register, but its behavior is not affected by the COMMAND.I2Cidle.\n\nSo per strict reading, even in sleep RAA needs to detect within [tCcStatusDelay(+modifiers)]. Capped in Type-C land, [tRpValueChange] (20ms max). Otherwise we start impinging on [tOnePortToggleConnect] (80ms max) timings, breaking spec timing variables and assumptions.\n\nA violation of that last case seems to be what is happening here. (RAA autotoggling, ServoV4p1 fixed SrcDTS.)",
